From: Saphira packaging <recipes@saphira.vm2.uk>
Subject: [PATCH] cfg_help: size the enumerator buffer for any size_t

"first".."tenth" cover idx<10; beyond that snprintf prints idx+1
(up to 20 digits + '.'). A 10-byte buffer trips
-Wformat-truncation. 32 bytes holds any 64-bit value with margin;
stack-local, no behavior change.

--- a/src-api/config/cfg_help.c
+++ b/src-api/config/cfg_help.c
@@ -273,7 +273,7 @@
 cfg_help_token(struct autobuf *out, bool preamble, const struct cfg_schema_entry *token_entry,
   const struct cfg_schema_entry *sub_entries, size_t entry_count,
   const struct cfg_schema_token_customizer *customizer) {
-  char enum_buffer[10];
+  char enum_buffer[32];
   size_t i;
